  "reconstruction": "Generate the 2026-09-30 mass-failure calibration fixture (design \u00a75.A5).\n\nReads the forensics bundle and emits a COMPACT json (only the fields the rescue\npredicate reads) so the committed fixture stays small. Provenance is recorded in\nthe emitted file itself.\n\nReconstruction, stated plainly because it is a reconstruction and not a replay:\n* deaths: per-session commit times from REPORT.md; the nine victims whose line in\n  the bundle carries no clock are placed inside their own seq bracket\n  (51710-51721 \u2192 20:00:12 .. 20:00:23) and marked ``\"death_at_source\":\n  \"interpolated\"`` (the exact second is not load-bearing: every one of the 21 is\n  > 30 s and < 1 h before the pass).\n* liveness at the pass: the snapshot is 20:04:46, AFTER Aida's manual resumes\n  (20:03:28+), so 8 victims read ``live`` there. The fixture models a pass at\n  20:02:45 \u2014 before any recovery \u2014 so ALL 21 victims are dead (no live record)\n  and every non-victim is live. ``\"live_at_pass\"`` records that decision.\n* completion rows: ``completion_kind``/``completion_reason`` as the snapshot\n  carries them (the durable attention.db row); survivors keep theirs, which is\n  the point of the liveness-precedence test (they hold stale error rows while\n  running fine).\n* markers/levers: all 21 victims had NO runtime-stop.json and (for the 10\n  user-stop ones) no wake entry \u2014 verified in the design \u00a71.3; recorded as false.\n* ``created_at``: from cross-tab.csv.\n* pids: the snapshot's own, EXCEPT where it records 0/absent (two sessions carry\n  pid 0) \u2014 a duplicated pid makes two records collide in one ``<pid>.json``, so\n  those get a synthesized unique pid and ``\"pid_source\": \"synthesized\"``.\n",
  "source": "sessions-all-200446.json + cross-tab.csv + REPORT.md (attention.db seq 51708-51738)",
